# Frontend Conventions (Next.js + Bulletproof React)

Follow the [Bulletproof React](https://github.com/alan2207/bulletproof-react) architecture.

## Directory Structure

```
src/
├── app/              # Next.js App Router — pages and layouts only
├── components/
│   ├── ui/           # Primitive UI components (Button, Input, Modal…)
│   └── layout/       # App-level layout components (Header, Sidebar…)
├── features/         # Feature modules (self-contained)
│   └── <feature>/
│       ├── components/
│       ├── hooks/
│       ├── api/
│       ├── types/
│       └── stores/
├── hooks/            # Shared global hooks
├── lib/              # Third-party library configs (e.g. axios instance)
├── stores/           # Global state
├── types/            # Global TypeScript types
└── utils/            # Utility functions
```

## Rules

- Keep pages thin — delegate logic to `features/` or `hooks/`
- Co-locate everything related to a feature inside `features/<feature>/`
- Do not import across features directly; lift shared code to `components/` or `hooks/`
- Use named exports for components
